# Error toasts

These are product mandates, not optional UX suggestions.

## Failures use an error toast

- A failed user action shows `toast({ tone: 'error', title, description })` from `@/components/ui/toast`.
- Do not render the failure as inline page text.
- The title says what failed. The description is the specific message.

## Edge Function errors

- `supabase.functions.invoke` on a non-2xx response sets `error.message` to `Edge Function returned a non-2xx status code`. The function JSON sits on `error.context`.
- Read that body and toast its `error` string. Do not toast the generic status line.
